Project source licensing is mapped in LICENSING.md. Existing file-level notices
are preserved. This project is an independent implementation; it is not an
NVIDIA or ASUS release.

External inputs are acquired locally and are not included in Git:
- NVIDIA Windows ARM64 driver 617.42 and extracted firmware/runtime libraries.
- NVIDIA TensorRT 11.4 DLA compilers and Linux cuDLA 13.4.92 frontend.
- Board-specific ASUS/NVIDIA BIOS ROM captures.
Their original distribution terms and notices remain with those inputs.

Protocol research uses NVIDIA-authored Jetson linux-nv-oot sources and the open
NVDLA project as references. Exact revisions and URLs are recorded in docs/.
The linux-nv-oot implementation is GPL-2.0-only; existing GPL declarations in
this repository are retained. Generated vendor disassembly/decompiler exports
stay in ignored results/ and are not distributed here.

Super-resolution source model:
  ONNX Model Zoo, sub_pixel_cnn_2016 / super-resolution-10.onnx
  https://github.com/onnx/models/tree/main/validated/vision/super_resolution/sub_pixel_cnn_2016
  The model’s source README identifies Apache-2.0. The model is downloaded
  separately, hash-checked and kept in ignored sources/.

Included demo photograph and measured result:
  NASA photograph of astronaut Eileen Collins, distributed by scikit-image
  as data.astronaut (documented there as public domain).
  https://scikit-image.org/docs/stable/api/skimage.data.html#skimage.data.astronaut
  https://github.com/scikit-image/scikit-image/blob/v0.19.3/skimage/data/astronaut.png
  demo/assets/astronaut-input.png is the unchanged acquired sample.
  demo/assets/astronaut-dla-3x.png is the actual measured N1X DLA output.
  File hashes and processing provenance are recorded in demo/assets/README.md
  and docs/evidence/npu-hardware-2026-10-28.json. No model weights or vendor
  loadables are included with the images.

